# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Panda Numbers - PRODUCTION build configuration (Vite loads this for
# `vite build`; `npm run dev` ignores it, so local development keeps using the
# Vite proxy on http://127.0.0.1:8787).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The deployed backend (Render). It is a PUBLIC URL - it appears in every
# request the browser makes - never a secret.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# The app is served as static files by Vercel, which has no /api routes: an
# unset API URL makes `/api/auth/login` hit `https://<app>.vercel.app`, get
# answered with index.html, and the login page reports
#   "This build has no API URL configured, so the sign-in request went to the
#    website host instead of the API."
# A Vercel Environment Variable only reaches a build created AFTER it is saved,
# so a missing variable silently produced a build that could never log in.
# This file is committed, so every build has a real API host.
#
# An explicit Vercel environment variable (VITE_API_URL / VITE_API_BASE_URL /
# VITE_BACKEND_URL) still wins - Vite gives real environment variables priority
# over .env files - so changing the backend needs no code edit.
VITE_API_URL=https://pandanumbers-api.onrender.com
